    "result_text": "The build is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that rejects creating an owner when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners, responding with HTTP 409.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **New exception** \u2014 `rest/advice/OwnerCityCapacityExceededException.java`, following the same shape as the existing `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` / `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException` conflict exceptions.\n\n2. **Exception handler** \u2014 added `handleOwnerCityCapacityExceededException` to `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, mapping the new exception to a `409 CONFLICT` `ProblemDetail` with `errors: [\"city\"]`, matching the existing 409 handlers.\n\n3. **Controller check** \u2014 in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, added a `rejectCityAtCapacity(...)` call (right after required-field validation) plus a `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 50` constant and a helper that counts existing owners in the same city. City matching reuses the existing `normalizeHouseholdField` normalization (trim/collapse-whitespace/lowercase), consistent with how city is already compared in `generateCustomerCode`, so cosmetic case/spacing differences count as the same city.\n\nVerification: the full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` case that fills a fresh city to exactly 50 owners and asserts the 51st create returns 409.",
